2.1)HTML

a)HTML basics

📅 Last Updated: 17 Jul, 2025**

🔹 What is HTML?

 HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is the **standard language** for creating and structuring web pages.
 Defines layout using **elements and tags** for text, images, links, and multimedia.
 Used in **95%+ of all websites**, making it essential for modern web development.
 Core components: **tags, attributes, elements, and document structure**.


 🔹 HTML Basic Document & Structure

 Every document starts with `<!DOCTYPE html>` → defines document type.
 Main structural tags:

   `<html>` → root element.
   `<head>` → contains metadata (title, stylesheets, meta tags).
   `<title>` → defines page title (appears in browser tab).
   `<body>` → contains visible content (text, images, videos, links).

Example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>HTML</title>
</head>
<body>
  <p>GeeksforGeeks is an online study platform</p>
</body>
</html>
```

---

🔹 HTML Headings

 Tags: `<h1>` to `<h6>` (largest to smallest).
 Used to create a **hierarchy of text importance**.

Syntax Example:

```html
<h1>Heading 1</h1>
<h6>Heading 6</h6>
```

---

🔹 HTML Paragraphs & Breaks

 `<p>` → defines a paragraph.
`<br>` → inserts a line break (empty tag).

Example:

```html
<p>HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.<br>
It is used to design web pages.<br></p>
```

---

### 🔹 HTML Horizontal Line

* `<hr>` → creates a horizontal rule to divide sections.
* Empty tag, no closing required.

**Example:**

```html
<p>Content above</p>
<hr>
<p>Content below</p>
```

---

### 🔹 HTML Comments

* Used for notes, explanations, or disabling code.
* Not displayed in browser.

**Syntax:**

```html
<!-- Single-line comment -->
<!-- 
  Multi-line 
  comment 
-->
```

**Best Practices:**

* Keep comments concise and relevant.
* Avoid over-commenting obvious code.
* Update comments when code changes.

---

### 🔹 HTML Images

* `<img>` → inserts an image.
* `src` attribute defines the image source.
* Can include `alt` (alternative text) for accessibility.

**Syntax Example:**

```html
<img src="geeks.png" alt="GeeksforGeeks Logo">
```

---

### 🔹 Viewing HTML Source Code

1. **Entire page**: `Ctrl + U` or right-click → *View Page Source*.
2. **Specific element**: Right-click → *Inspect*. Allows editing & testing live changes.

---

### 🔹 Conclusion

* HTML is the **foundation of web development**.
* Learning basic tags and structure lets you build functional, organized web pages.
* With practice, you can create interactive and optimized websites.

---
