F)HTML Tables:-

Here’s a **concise revision-friendly note for HTML Tables**:

---

## **HTML Tables – Revision Notes**

### **1. Basic Structure**

* `<table>` → defines the table.
* `<tr>` → table row.
* `<th>` → table header (bold, centered by default).
* `<td>` → table data (cell content).
* **Example:**

```html
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Firstname</th>
    <th>Lastname</th>
    <th>Age</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Priya</td>
    <td>Sharma</td>
    <td>24</td>
  </tr>
</table>
```

---

### **2. HTML Table Tags**

| Tag          | Description                  |
| ------------ | ---------------------------- |
| `<table>`    | Creates a table              |
| `<tr>`       | Defines a row                |
| `<th>`       | Header cell                  |
| `<td>`       | Data cell                    |
| `<caption>`  | Table title                  |
| `<thead>`    | Table header section         |
| `<tbody>`    | Main content section         |
| `<tfoot>`    | Footer section               |
| `<col>`      | Attributes for columns       |
| `<colgroup>` | Group columns for formatting |

---

### **3. Styling Tables (CSS)**

1. **Borders**

```css
table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; }
```

2. **Collapsed Borders**

```css
table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; }
```

3. **Cell Padding**

```css
th, td { padding: 20px; }
```

4. **Text Alignment**

```css
th { text-align: left; }
```

5. **Border Spacing**

```css
table { border-spacing: 5px; }
```

6. **Background Color**

```css
table#t01 { background-color: #f2f2d1; }
```

---

### **4. Span Cells**

* **Colspan:** Merge multiple columns

```html
<th colspan="2">Telephone</th>
```

* **Rowspan:** Merge multiple rows

```html
<th rowspan="2">Telephone</th>
```

---

### **5. Captions**

* Add table title:

```html
<caption>DETAILS</caption>
```

---

### **6. Nested Tables**

* A table inside another table:

```html
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>Outer Table</td>
    <td>
      <table>
        <tr><td>Inner Table Row1</td></tr>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
```

---

G)HTML Attributes:-

Here’s a **concise revision-friendly note for HTML Attributes**:

---

## **HTML Attributes – Revision Notes**

### **1. Definition**

* Special words within an opening tag that define additional info about an element.
* Syntax:

```html
<tagname attribute_name="attribute_value">content</tagname>
```

* Example:

```html
<img src="image.png" alt="Logo">
```

* **Components:**

  1. **attribute_name** → name of property (e.g., src, href, id)
  2. **attribute_value** → value assigned to attribute, always in quotes.

---

### **2. Types of Attributes**

**A. Global Attributes** (usable on any element):

| Attribute       | Purpose                                  |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| id              | Unique identifier for CSS/JS targeting   |
| class           | Group elements for styling               |
| style           | Inline CSS styling                       |
| title           | Tooltip text on hover                    |
| lang            | Language of element content              |
| tabindex        | Keyboard navigation order                |
| role            | Accessibility role                       |
| contenteditable | Editable content                         |
| href            | Link destination (for `<a>` element)     |
| src             | Resource location (images, video, audio) |
| alt             | Alternative text for images              |

**B. Other Types**

* Event attributes → handle events like onclick, onmouseover.
* Input attributes → specific to `<input>` inside `<form>`.
* Image attributes → specific to `<img>`.
* Link attributes → specific to `<a>` and `<link>`.
* Table attributes → `<table>`, `<tr>`, `<th>`, `<td>`.
* Media attributes → `<audio>`, `<video>`.
* Accessibility attributes → `alt`, `aria-*`.
* Meta attributes → `<meta>` like charset, viewport.

---

### **3. Common HTML Attributes Examples**

1. **alt** → alternative text for images:

```html
<img src="image.png" alt="Logo">
```

2. **width & height** → set image dimensions:

```html
<img src="image.png" width="300" height="100">
```

3. **id** → unique identifier:

```html
<h1 id="header">Hello</h1>
```

4. **title** → tooltip text:

```html
<h3 title="Hello GeeksforGeeks">Hover here</h3>
```

5. **href** → hyperlink destination:

```html
<a href="https://example.com" target="_blank">Visit</a>
```

6. **style** → inline CSS styling:

```html
<h2 style="color:#8CCEF9; text-align:center;">Hello</h2>
```

7. **lang** → language declaration:

```html
<p lang="en">Text in English</p>
<p lang="fr">Texte en français</p>
```

---

### **4. Important Points**

1. **Lowercase Attributes** → Recommended (W3C).
2. **Quote Attribute Values** → Always use quotes `" "` for consistency.
3. **Quotes Inside Values** → Use single quotes if value has double quotes:

```html
<input placeholder='Enter "username" here'>
```

4. **Boolean Attributes** → Write without value:

```html
<input type="checkbox" checked>
```

5. **Attribute Order (Readability)** → Common order: id → class → global → specific → event

```html
<button id="btn1" class="btn" type="submit" onclick="handleClick()">Submit</button>
```

6. **Avoid Deprecated Attributes** → e.g., `align`, `bgcolor`, `border`. Use CSS instead.

---

This covers **all essential HTML attribute concepts** for **quick revision**.

